<title>BELGIUM: Belgian GEC Alsthom unit in 2 bln bfr tram order.</title>
<headline>Belgian GEC Alsthom unit in 2 bln bfr tram order.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLEROI, Belgium 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>ACEC Transport, part of the GEC Alsthom  ALSF.CN group, said on Tuesday it won a two billion Belgian franc order from the Brussels public transport network MIVB/STIB for 12 trams.</p>
<p>ACEC Transport spokesman Luc Topet told Reuters the order represented two years' work for the company.</p>
<p>ACEC Transport is one of three units of GEC Alsthom, a joint venture between France's Alcatel Alsthom and Britain's GEC plc. The others are electro-mechanical company  Celegec ACEC and ACEC Energie.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
